# --- CYBERPUN-16-1-t2: asset-pack import scratch/exclusions ---
# code_materialize_attachment can only safe-extract a WHOLE zip attachment
# (it cannot select a single member), and there is no tool in this workspace
# that can move/rename a freshly-extracted, not-yet-tracked binary file. Each
# extraction therefore lands ALL 33 pack entries under its dest_path. These
# rules keep the surplus entries (and one accidental early extraction) out of
# the committed tree; see CLAUDE.md/AGENT.md "Asset pack import" for the
# referencing scheme this forces on the two `_ImportedPack/` roots.
/tmp_assets_extract/
/tmp_probe/
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/probe.txt
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/probe2.txt
# accidental first-pass extraction directly into an imageset folder (superseded
# by the Sprites/_ImportedPack + Buildings/_ImportedPack scheme below)
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Sprites/sprite_player_walk.imageset/assets/
# never-imported pack contents (docs/bootstrap.md "Explicitly deferred"):
# the structure-only tileset, and the screens/ UI mockups
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Sprites/_ImportedPack/assets/screens/
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Sprites/_ImportedPack/assets/pixelgrit/tileset_structure.png
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Sprites/_ImportedPack/assets/pixelgrit/buildings/
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Buildings/_ImportedPack/assets/screens/
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Buildings/_ImportedPack/assets/pixelgrit/tileset_structure.png
CyberpunkMonsterCrawl/Assets.xcassets/Buildings/_ImportedPack/assets/pixelgrit/*.png
